+# DOSBox-X — win1-op debug fork
+
+This is a debug fork of DOSBox-X for the win1-op project,
+based on upstream DOSBox-X `66480b4a84c9adc8002f21b332da8f694a9978c4`.
+It is not required to run win1-op; it adds the control and tracing tools used
+while reverse-engineering and testing Windows 1.01.
+
+The changes are on `master` (and the equivalent `win1-op-debug` branch).
+
+## Added in this fork
+
+- **MCP control channel** — a raw POSIX socket owned by the emulation thread,
+  with `PING`, `BREAK`, `EXEC`, `BP`, `BPINT`, `BPM` and headless events.
+- **`LOGSEGLOAD seg:off`** — log every Windows `SEGLOAD` call/return, with the
+  module name, to `SEGLOAD.TXT` without stopping the CPU.
+- **`LOGB [n]`** — binary per-instruction delta trace to `LOGCPU.BIN`
+  (CS:IP, changed-register mask, changed values) for long drawing traces.
+- **`MOUSEMOVE dx dy` / `MOUSEBUTTON 1|0`** — inject relative serial-mouse
+  movement and button state while tracing.
+- **Memory / NE inspection** — `MEMDUMPASC`, `MEMCMP`, `MEMFINDSTR`,
+  `MEMFINDHEX`, `NEDUMP` and `WINSCAN`.
+- **`SAVESTATE` / `LOADSTATE`** — full emulator state save and restore.
+- **Richer illegal-interrupt diagnostics** — print the faulting `CS:IP` and
+  `SS:SP`.
+- **Monitor guards** — fail a TCP listen cleanly instead of leaving a null
+  `_server`, and guard a null listener thread.
+
+See [WIN1-OP-DEBUG.md](WIN1-OP-DEBUG.md) for the commands and build flags.
+
+## Original DOSBox-X README
+
+The upstream README follows unchanged below.
+
+---
+
 
 **Welcome to the DOSBox-X project homepage located on GitHub.**
 
