+# win1-op debug harness
+
+This fork adds the DeepSeek Harness / win1-op debugging features to
+DOSBox-X at upstream `66480b4a8` (2026-10-29). It is a test/debug fork, not a
+runtime dependency of the win1-op release. The changes are merged to
+`master`; the `win1-op-debug` branch points at the same commit.
+
+## What was added
+
+| feature | purpose |
+|---|---|
+| MCP control channel | raw POSIX socket owned by the emulation thread; `PING`, `BREAK`, `EXEC`, `BP`, `BPINT`, `BPM`, headless events |
+| `DEBUG_MCP_*` break/headless entry points | stop/continue without an attached SDL window |
+| `LOGSEGLOAD seg:off` | log every Windows `SEGLOAD` call/return with the module name to `SEGLOAD.TXT`, without stopping the CPU |
+| `LOGB [n]` | binary per-instruction delta trace to `LOGCPU.BIN` (CS:IP, changed-register mask, changed values) |
+| `MOUSEMOVE dx dy` | inject relative serial-mouse movement while tracing |
+| `MOUSEBUTTON 1\|0` | inject left button down/up while tracing |
+| memory/NEDUMP commands | `MEMDUMPASC`, `MEMCMP`, `MEMFINDSTR`, `MEMFINDHEX`, `NEDUMP`, `WINSCAN` |
+| `SAVESTATE` / `LOADSTATE` | full emulator state save/restore |
+| richer illegal-interrupt log | print the faulting `CS:IP` and `SS:SP` |
+| monitor null-server guard | return failure when the TCP listen fails instead of leaving a null `_server`; guard a null listener thread |
+
+The monitor's empty/`off` handling was already improved upstream; this branch
+keeps that version and only adds the null-`_server`/null-thread guard.
+
+## Build
+
+```sh
+./autogen.sh
+(cd vs/sdl && ./build-dosbox.sh)
+(cd vs/sdlnet && ./build-dosbox.sh)
+CFLAGS='-g3 -O0 -fno-inline -fno-omit-frame-pointer' \
+CXXFLAGS='-g3 -O0 -fno-inline -fno-omit-frame-pointer' \
+./configure --enable-debug=heavy --disable-dynamic-core --disable-optimize \
+    --prefix=/usr
+make -j48
+```
+
+The binary is `src/dosbox-x`. `C_DEBUG` and `C_HEAVY_DEBUG` are enabled.
+
+## Notes
+
+* `LOGB` is the compact trace format used by win1-op for long drawing traces;
+  `work/decode_logb.py` in the parent workspace decodes it.
+* `LOGSEGLOAD` output is parsed by `work/parse_loadmap.py` to get runtime
+  segment bases.
+* MCP is a raw POSIX socket; the fork exists because the upstream TCP monitor
+  and the SDLNet-based control path were not reliable enough for repeated
+  attach/detach during tracing.
+* This branch is GPL-2.0-or-later, like DOSBox-X. The win1-op release's MIT
+  license does not apply to it.
